M02_Respawn_Controller::Custom indexes its M02_AREACOUNT (26) per-area arrays
with the custom parameter. Retail M02.mix binds M02_Nod_Soldier "99,0,2" to the
start-cinematic soldiers 401002 and 401003; their timer registers area 99 with
custom 103 and their self-destruct reports custom 101. area_unit_count[99] is
73 bytes past the end of the 26-byte array and lands in the high byte of
area_officer[11], so the original code wrote outside the array while those
soldiers lived. Ignore the area-indexed customs (101-109, 114) whose area is
outside the arrays. Every in-range area keeps its original handling, and the
non-indexed customs (111, 112, 113, 115, 116) are unchanged.

--- a/Mission02.cpp
+++ b/Mission02.cpp
@@ -3135,6 +3135,15 @@

 	void Custom (GameObject *obj, int type, int param, GameObject *sender)
 	{
+		// Vita bounds: area-indexed customs must stay inside the M02_AREACOUNT
+		// arrays. Retail start-cinematic soldiers register area 99, which the
+		// original code wrote past the end of area_unit_count.
+		if ((((type >= 101) && (type <= 109)) || (type == 114)) &&
+			((param < 0) || (param >= M02_AREACOUNT)))
+		{
+			return;
+		}
+
 		if (type == 101)
 		{
 			// A unit has died, subtract him from his area (param).
